35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I found that... we lose an hour every day just copying records. And there are delivery errors because of inconsistent addresses.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"Oh, this is just as I feared. The coordination group is a ghost town, yet the work is still getting done by a few exhausted souls.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,How predictable. Our customer plants have terrible network coverage and the visitor approval process is a nightmare. We're planning for a fantasy world.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The capital budget is frozen. Any proposal requiring a large upfront investment is dead. However, the recurring software allowance is available.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Guys, listen! The big, fancy projects that everyone had to use just died. Only the small, specific tools for one group actually survived!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,@Kenji... so the small things work better? Maybe we should focus on those daily losses I mentioned.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, only if it doesn't mean more manual work for the coordination group. They are already at a breaking point.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, if the budget is frozen, we can't afford a massive overhaul. And with the site access issues, any ""on-site"" deployment is a gamble.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Precisely. We must avoid per-head licensing. If the cost scales with the user base, we will face a crisis during next year's renewal.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,Exactly! We shouldn't try to save the whole company at once. We need something that solves a real problem for a small group.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I really think the copying records thing is a waste. It's a small pain, but it happens every single day.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,I'm looking at the developer side too. Our in-house guys are gone until Q3. Any project needing custom code is a non-starter.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, that's the nail in the coffin for the ambitious ones. We need a solution that is vendor-managed and doesn't require on-site setup.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I will only support a proposal that fits within the software allowance and has a predictable, fixed cost. No scaling licenses.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm with Ryuji! Let's pick the one that is most likely to actually be used in a year, not just the one that looks best on a slide.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
